  "alternateName": [
    "Neuro-JEPA training and evaluation code"
  ],
  "description": "Reference implementation for Neuro-JEPA, a sparse latent predictive foundation model for multimodal volumetric brain MRI that extends V-JEPA 2 to 3D with a Mixture-of-Experts backbone. The repository provides pretraining, fine-tuning, and evaluation code for T1w/T2w/FLAIR neuroimaging, including foreground-aware masking strategies and the 47-task downstream evaluation harness described in the paper. Python (PyTorch). The code is MIT-licensed; the associated pretrained model weights are released separately under a gated, non-commercial CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0 licence.",
